
preimage in preimages.jl
Decide what is the best behavior


BasisDefinition opnormbound, normbound
Failing due to a delicate issue, while L1 is a subtype of NormKind,  Type{L1} is not a subtype of Type{NormKind}

AnnulusGeometry.jl, EllipseGeometry.jl: enclose T on the boundary path by Taylor models
The boundary checks evaluate T directly on boxes covering the arcs.  TaylorModels 0.10 has
elementary functions (exp, sin, cos, ...) on real models only: on a complex model exp fails
(no _rpa method for Complex{Interval}).  Route: carry Re T and Im T on the line Im x = b as
two real TaylorModel1 in x, which needs T given by its two parts.  Further: TaylorModels
with BallArithmetic coefficients, and complex rpa.


TransferTaylorModels.jl: avoid the one-float cells of transfer_taylor_models on a piecewise f.
When the image T(c') of an input cell boundary is a non-thin enclosure, the cell it gives
is one or two floats wide and gets a constant model.  Two options, which combine:
- overlapping models: build each cell model on its cell enlarged by a margin delta inside
  the piece between cuts; when delta exceeds the width of the enclosure of T(c'), the
  preimage of an output cell lies in one enlarged input cell, and no cut at T(c') is needed;
- a floating-point representable partition: round T(c') to a nearby float y*; between y*
  and the true T(c') the preimage lies just past c', so the neighbouring model must hold a
  few floats beyond its cell (the overlap above, with a margin of one or two floats).
